WEBVTT

00:05:54.127 --> 00:06:00.198
I grew up in a family where all of that
was really normal and par for the course,

00:06:00.222 --> 00:06:03.512
and I became aware at a pretty early age

00:06:03.536 --> 00:06:08.124
that my preference of how
I liked to spend my time

00:06:08.148 --> 00:06:09.485
didn't always match up

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:13.633
with the way people thought
that kids were supposed to be.

00:06:13.657 --> 00:06:16.712
You know, there was this feeling
that you'd want to get together

00:06:16.736 --> 00:06:20.095
in a group of kids and sing a song,

00:06:20.119 --> 00:06:22.129
just this kind of constant socializing.

00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:25.991
CA: Were there lots of awkward
or painful moments as a child,

00:06:26.015 --> 00:06:28.608
where you were just, "No,
please don't make me do that.

00:06:28.632 --> 00:06:30.409
I don't want to go to that party,"